# Mesen action vocabulary (infer when possible)

When the user names a high-level action, translate it to controller + frames without asking for bit masks unless ambiguous.

## Throw (carryable / Luigi)

- **Meaning**: release grab while optionally holding a direction so Mario throws Luigi (or Luigi throws a held item).
- **Input**: clear grab buttons **Y and X** (`$15` y-bit / `$17` x-bit). Hold **Right** or **Left** if they want directional throw momentum.
- **Do not** hold Y/X across the resume — that keeps carrying.
- **Default script**: `tools/test/mesen/run-throw-luigi.ps1` (Right + release grab, ~30 frames).
- **Watch**: Luigi `14C8` `$0B`→`$09`/`$0A`, sprite X speed `B6`, Y speed `AA` (SA-1 `!AA` = `$9E`), freeram `PreviousXSpeed` `$41B835`, `BouncingSpeed` `$41A023`, `LandingTimer` `$41B834`.

## Swap / teleport (L or R)

- **Meaning**: player and Luigi sprite swap places (`$18` L/R bits `$30`). Identity flips (`!IsMario` `$41A026`).
- **Items**: `TransferItems` swaps holdings — Mario’s item → `!LuigiHeldItemIndex` (`$41B82E`, status `$09`), Luigi’s item → `!MarioHeldItemIndex` (`$41B82F`, status `$0B`). During the TP anim both are hidden as status `$07` (Yoshi-mouth trick), then restored on exit.
- **Spin / jump**: at swap start, Luigi `!Spinning` `$41A00C` ← player `$140D`; `!JumpHeld` `$41A018` ← A/B on `$15`. On exit, player `$140D` ← `!TempSpinning`. Keep **A/B held** across swap if you want high bounce/`JumpHeld` after. Keep **spin** by swapping while `$140D` is set (spin jumping).
- **Grab (Y/X) during swap**: safe to hold. After swap, the **companion Luigi sprite** has the item you were holding (not the player). Holding Y does not keep the player carrying that item post-swap.
- **Disappear bug (UberASM)**: `MoveLuigiToFront` held-item sync must use SA-1 DP mirrors (`$30B6`/`$309E`/`$3094`/`$30D1`/`$307D`/`$3076`), not bare `$B6`/`$94`/`$D1`/`$7D`/`$76` — those are WRAM garbage on SNES-side UberASM and park the item at bogus X (e.g. `$7954`).
- **Do not** swap while carrying Luigi himself (`14C8=$0B` blocks teleport).
- **Mesen input**: L/R via `set_controller_input` `l`/`r`; grab via `y`/`x`.

## Other common actions

| Phrase | Input |
|---|---|
| walk / run right | Right held |
| jump | B (or A if they say spin — X+B context) |
| spin jump | typically X+B (confirm if unsure) |
| release grab / drop | Y=0, X=0 |

## Mesen process hygiene

- **Do not** kill/relaunch Mesen to pick up ROM ASM inserts — that drops MCP, SA-1 debugger, and savestate UI. Insert into `workspace/RHRv5.smc` on disk; ask the user to reload the ROM in Mesen (or power cycle in-emulator) when needed.
- Savestates: user creates them in Mesen; scripts load slot N via MCP. Prefer hex in all logs.
